From ucc1ef8c8158d6b73 at groups.google.com  Fri Oct 23 15:17:49 2015
From: ucc1ef8c8158d6b73 at groups.google.com (Yihui Xie)
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2015 15:17:49 +0000
Subject: Re: [knitr] knitr to pdf src image issue
Message-ID: <bFX5JKZPySA.aiR_T6OJDAAJ@knitr.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/knitr/c/bFX5JKZPySA/m/aiR_T6OJDAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

<img> is an HTML tag, and it is not portable in the sense that Pandoc
won't convert it to LaTeX. Only the Markdown syntax is portable, i.e.
![]() but you cannot set the alignment or size of the image when using
the Markdown syntax.

If the image is generated from an R plot, you can use chunk options
fig.align, fig.with/fig.height, out.width/out.height to set the
alignment/size, and knitr will automatically generate LaTeX or HTML
code according to the output format. That is a portable approach.

Regards,
Yihui
--
Yihui Xie <xiey...@gmail.com>
Web: http://yihui.name

